{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784248650236,"sessionID":"ses_0927f0a94ffe0MNkUI1qsEQ6A5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"skill","callID":"call_00_zLwYdecu1u5e5VICZMqh3821","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"name":"minecraft-production-design"},"output":"<skill_content name=\"minecraft-production-design\">\n# Skill: minecraft-production-design\n\n# Minecraft Production Design\n\n## Outputs\nLocation plan, asset register, risk register, build budget, and location cards.\n\n## Method\nStart from locked shots. Decide what must be in Minecraft, what may be Blender, and what can be implied through edit/sound. Pin versions and test the hardest technical bridge early. Build hero geometry, a modular kit, perceptual extensions, and editorial geography. Track provenance and reuse.\n\n## Constraint\nDo not design unseen world detail merely for completeness. Every expensive element needs shot IDs and a fallback.\n\nBase directory for this skill: K:\\Minecraft Narrative Studio\\.agents\\skills\\minecraft-production-design\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","metadata":{"name":"minecraft-production-design","dir":"K:\\Minecraft Narrative Studio\\.agents\\skills\\minecraft-production-design","truncated":false},"title":"Loaded skill: minecraft-production-design","time":{"start":1784248650171,"end":1784248650214}},"id":"prt_f6d81c93e0019NuzI1tHsaVwQl","sessionID":"ses_0927f0a94ffe0MNkUI1qsEQ6A5","messageID":"msg_f6d81b313001YNDY9KEqr68uAh"}}
